1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:00,980
Hi,

2
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:01,580
I'm Pip!

3
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,280
Ever wondered how sunshine

4
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:04,200
can light up a whole

5
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:04,480
city?

6
00:00:05,013 --> 00:00:06,640
It starts with tiny packets

7
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:07,900
of light called photons,

8
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:09,420
racing all the way from

9
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:09,800
the sun.

10
00:00:10,225 --> 00:00:11,560
When photons hit a solar

11
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,040
panel,

12
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:13,560
they knock electrons loose

13
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:14,540
inside the silicon.

14
00:00:15,019 --> 00:00:16,560
Those moving electrons make

15
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:17,540
an electric current.

16
00:00:17,901 --> 00:00:19,260
An inverter changes that

17
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:20,320
current into the kind our

18
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:21,200
homes can use.

19
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:23,180
Then power lines carry it

20
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:23,780
into town,

21
00:00:23,910 --> 00:00:25,060
and the whole city lights

22
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:25,330
up!

23
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:26,740
Sunlight in,

24
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:28,000
electricity out.

25
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:29,280
Pretty bright idea,

26
00:00:29,390 --> 00:00:29,700
right?
